  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 100 AM EDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nAs we head into the weekend and early into next week, the mid/upper \nlevel low will move into the Gulf, and higher moisture levels move \ninto the region. Light ESE flow this weekend will eventually become \nsoutherly by early next week. With deep tropical moisture moving \ninto South FL, higher than normal PoPs (80-90%) are expected each \nday. With generally weak steering flows expected along with \nefficient rainfall rates, urban and poor drainage flooding will \nlikely be the main threat each day. All of this will continue to be \ngood news for the ongoing improving drought conditions. \n\nTemperatures during the extended period will be right around normal \nwith highs generally in the upper 80s to lower 90s, and low temps in \nthe mid to upper 70s.",
